  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed a full set at the Open End Gallery in Chicago, Illinois, on Thursday, October 13, 2005 [1][2]. This specific performance is the 82nd of 467 archived shows for the band in the collection [2]. The recording, titled tmg2005-10-13.flac, was taped by Peter Sohriakoff and contains 16 songs with a total duration of 58 minutes [1]. The setlist begins with \"Color In Your Cheeks\" and \"Going to Cleveland,\" the latter of which is a rare entry with only eight archived performances [1][2]. The band also plays \"Spilling Toward Alpha,\" another rare track with six archived performances [1][2]. Other songs in the main set include \"Old College Try,\" \"Jenny,\" \"Twin Human Highway Flares,\" \"Grendel's Mother,\" \"Broom People,\" and \"Love Love Love\" [1]. Franklin Bruno joins on piano for \"Song For Dennis Brown,\" \"Mole,\" \"You Or Your Memory,\" \"Dance Music,\" and \"This Year\" [1]. The show concludes with an encore featuring \"California Song\" and \"No Children\" [1]. The previous archived show for the band was on October 12, 2005, at The Canopy Club [2]. This is the only available recording of this date, making it a complete capture of the evening's music [1].",
